## CDS View Naming (Quick Reference)

📚 **Full Guidelines**: See [docs/ABAP_Standards.md](../docs/ABAP_Standards.md) Section 3

### View Prefixes
```
I_<name>     Interface view (reusable, stable)
C_<name>     Consumption view (UI-specific)
A_<name>     External API view (published)
R_<name>     Restricted reuse view (with auth)
E_<name>     Extension include view
X_<name>     View extension
D_<name>     Abstract entity
```

### View Suffixes
```
Cube, C       Analytical cube
Query, Q      Analytical query
VH            Value help
Text, T       Text view
TP            Transactional processing
Draft, D      Draft view
HierNode, HN  Hierarchy node
```

### Naming Rules
- ✅ Use CamelCase (e.g., I_SalesOrder)
- ✅ Use singular form (not plural)
- ✅ No underscores between words
- ✅ Business semantic names
- ✅ Approved abbreviations only

---

## Anti-Patterns to AVOID

### ❌ 1. NOT NULL Preserving Left Outer Join (NNPLOJ)
```cds
// ❌ BAD: ELSE clause prevents null preservation
case
  when col3 = 'x' then 'y'
  else 'z'  // ❌ Forces join execution
end

// ✅ GOOD: No ELSE - allows null preservation
case
  when col3 = 'x' then 'y'
  // ✅ No ELSE
end
```

### ❌ 2. Union ALL in Left Outer Join (UALOJ)
```cds
// ❌ BAD: UNION in view used in LEFT OUTER JOIN
define view A as select from tbl1 { ... }
union all select from tbl2 { ... }  // ❌

// ✅ GOOD: Avoid UNION in joined views
```

### ❌ 3. Cyclic Joins
```cds
// ❌ BAD: Creates cycle
left outer join tbl2 on ...
inner join tbl3 on tbl3.col = tbl1.col
               and tbl3.col = tbl2.col  // ❌ Cycle

// ✅ GOOD: Use hint or restructure
@Consumption.dbHints: ['NO_CYCLIC_JOIN']
```

### ❌ 4. Calculated Fields in Wrong Places
```cds
// ❌ BAD: Calculated field in WHERE
where case when field2 = 'X' then 'Active' end = 'Active'

// ✅ GOOD: Filter on base field
where field2 = 'X'
```

### ❌ 5. Wrong Association Cardinality
```cds
// ❌ BAD: Wrong cardinality
association [0..*] to I_Customer  // Forces execution

// ✅ GOOD: Correct cardinality
association [0..1] to I_Customer  // Allows optimization
```

---

## Best Practices

### 1. View Structure

✅ **Build result set first, then join auxiliary data**:
```cds
// Step 1: Core data with filters
define view I_SalesOrderCore as select from vbak
{
  key vbeln as SalesOrder,
  erdat as CreationDate
}
where auart = 'OR';  // ✅ Filter early

// Step 2: Add auxiliary data via associations
define view I_SalesOrder as select from I_SalesOrderCore
  association [0..1] to I_Customer as _Customer
    on $projection.SoldToParty = _Customer.Customer
{
  key SalesOrder,
  CreationDate,
  _Customer.CustomerName  // ✅ Join auxiliary data last
}
```

### 2. Field Exposure

✅ **Expose only required fields**:
```cds
// ❌ BAD
{ * }  // Exposes all fields

// ✅ GOOD
{
  key matnr as Material,
  mtart as MaterialType,
  matkl as MaterialGroup
  // Only fields actually needed
}
```

### 3. Associations

✅ **Use associations for optional fields**:
```cds
association [0..1] to I_Customer as _Customer
  on $projection.Customer = _Customer.Customer
  and $projection.SalesOrg = _Customer.SalesOrg  // ✅ All shared fields
```

✅ **Always specify cardinality**:
- Prefer `[0..1]` over `[0..*]`
- Use `[1..1]` for mandatory relationships
- Use `[0..*]` only when truly many

### 4. Calculated Fields

✅ **Use calculated fields only as projected fields**:
```cds
{
  key field1,
  field2,
  // ✅ Calculated field as projection
  case
    when field2 = 'X' then 'Active'
    else 'Inactive'
  end as Status
}
where field2 = 'X';  // ✅ Filter on base field, not calculated
```

