## Performance Checklist

### Before Creating CDS View
- [ ] Performance annotations defined (@ObjectModel.usageType)
- [ ] Complexity < 100 tables (< 10 for Quality A)
- [ ] Only required fields exposed
- [ ] Associations used for optional fields
- [ ] No calculated fields in keys/filters/joins
- [ ] Naming follows VDM CDS guidelines

### During Development
- [ ] Test with realistic data volumes
- [ ] Measure response times (< 100ms for Quality A)
- [ ] Check for anti-patterns
- [ ] Validate with ATC checks (BC_CDS_PF1, PFCDS_QLTY)
- [ ] Analyze with PlanViz if needed

### Before Production
- [ ] All tests passing
- [ ] Performance thresholds met
- [ ] No anti-patterns detected
- [ ] Documentation complete
- [ ] ATC checks clean

---

## Service Quality Guidelines

### Quality A (Excellent)
**Use For**: High-volume transactions, frequent access
- Max ~10 underlying tables
- Response time: < 100ms
- Memory: < 1 GB
- Test with production volumes

### Quality B (Good)
**Use For**: Transactional Fiori apps, moderate volume
- Max ~20 underlying tables
- Response time: < 500ms
- Memory: < 2 GB
- Test with realistic data

### Quality C (Acceptable)
**Use For**: Analytical queries, lower volume
- Max ~50 underlying tables
- Response time: < 2s
- Memory: < 5 GB
- Test with representative data

---

## CDS View Template

```cds
@AbapCatalog.viewEnhancementCategory: [#NONE]
@AccessControl.authorizationCheck: #CHECK
@EndUserText.label: 'Sales Order'
@Metadata.ignorePropagatedAnnotations: true
@ObjectModel.usageType:{
  serviceQuality: #A,        // ✅ Choose based on use case
  sizeCategory: #L,          // ✅ Based on data volume
  dataClass: #TRANSACTIONAL  // ✅ Based on data type
}
define view entity I_SalesOrder
  as select from vbak
  association [0..1] to I_Customer as _Customer
    on $projection.SoldToParty = _Customer.Customer
{
  key vbeln as SalesOrder,
  erdat as CreationDate,
  kunnr as SoldToParty,
  netwr as NetAmount,
  
  // Associations
  _Customer
}
where auart = 'OR'  // ✅ Filter early
```

